      "advertiser": "ChatGPT for Education",
      "description": "“Our students deserve to be early participants in the future, not late recipients.”\n\nThat conviction has guided Lynwood Unified School District’s work with AI. Superintendent Patrick Gittisriboongul set the district-wide vision, while leaders, faculty, and staff have shaped how it takes form across their schools.\n\nIn 2023, Lynwood formed an AI task force, established local guardrails, and developed a roadmap. After joining OpenAI’s first K–12 cohort, its educators and leaders participated in training, office hours, feedback sessions, and conversations with peers from other districts.\n\nAt Marco Antonio Firebaugh High School, teachers have had time to learn and experiment. They use ChatGPT to get started on lesson plans, differentiate materials, review data, communicate with families, and work through recurring tasks—while retaining responsibility for every decision and final result.\nWe’re grateful to Lynwood’s educators and leaders for sharing what they’re learning and allowing us to learn alongside them.\n\nWatch Lynwood’s story, and read more about the districts bringing ChatGPT for Teachers to their educators: https://lnkd.in/gYgRC8p2",
