      "headline": "Introducing Three New Education Plugins",
      "startDate": null,
      "targeting": {},
      "adDuration": "",
      "advertiser": "ChatGPT for Education",
      "description": "Teaching and learning involve high-context work. An engaging lesson, course activity, or study plan depends on the right materials, audience, and goal.\n\nThat’s why we’re introducing three new education plugins for ChatGPT Work and Codex:\n\n• K-12 Educator\n• College Educator\n• College Student\n\nBuilt with feedback from educators and students, the plugins are designed to support the everyday work of teaching and learning while keeping you in control. Each brings together apps, role-specific skills, instructions, and common workflows so you can get started immediately, without constructing complex prompts on your own.\n\nBy connecting the tools and materials you already rely on, from documents and course materials to calendars and other approved apps, the plugins bring relevant context into the work. They can help students and educators move from curiosity to practice, lesson ideas to classroom materials, and project concepts to execution.\n\n• Educators can develop lessons, differentiate activities, prepare communications, and create engaging materials grounded in their course context.\n• College students can build study plans, practice concepts, and get support tailored to their courses.\n\nThe K-12 Educator plugin also connects to Learning Commons, which provides state academic standards and the detailed learning components and progressions beneath them, bringing the educational context behind the work into the conversation.\n\nGetting started is simple: call on a plugin with @ and ask it what it can do. Each one offers relevant agentic workflows in ChatGPT Work and Codex to help educators and college students get to a useful starting point faster.\n\nPlugins are now available in ChatGPT Edu and ChatGPT for Teachers district deployments.\n\nWe can’t wait to see what you build!\n\nLearn more here. https://lnkd.in/gTrWvHqb",
